  "issue_title": "Add a network-wide stake-transfers leaderboard to the explorer page",
  "issue_body": "## Context\n\n`GET /api/v1/chain/stake-transfers` is live and fully implemented \u2014 a between-coldkeys stake-transfer leaderboard computed from the `account_events` `StakeTransferred` stream (`src/chain-stake-transfers.mjs`, wired in `workers/api.mjs:2166` and `workers/request-handlers/analytics.mjs:1798-1848`, documented in `src/contracts.mjs:3087-3091`). It ranks subnets by StakeTransferred activity over a 7d/30d window, distinct from the already-planned within-account re-delegation churn leaderboard (`/chain/stake-moves`, #3468). The explorer page (`apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx`, 520 lines) has zero touchpoint for this data today \u2014 it renders daily activity, fees/tips, call mix, and top signers/fee-payers, but no stake-transfer leaderboard.\n\n## Requirement\n\nRender a network-wide stake-transfer leaderboard section on the chain explorer page (`/explorer`) \u2014 a per-subnet ranked table (StakeTransferred event count, distinct senders, transfers-per-sender) plus the network rollup, sharing the page's existing `7d`/`30d` window toggle.\n\n## Backend\n\n- Endpoint: `GET /api/v1/chain/stake-transfers?window=7d|30d&limit=N`\n- Query function: **none exists.** `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` has `subnetStakeTransfersQuery` (line 3074) for the **per-subnet** drill-in only \u2014 no query function calls `/api/v1/chain/stake-transfers`, and no `ChainStakeTransfers` type exists in `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts`. This PR must add the typed query function (following the `queryOptions`/`apiFetch`/normalize pattern already used for the sibling network-wide `chainTransferPairsQuery`, `queries.ts:2439-2458`) **and** the `ChainStakeTransfers` type, **as well as** the UI wiring \u2014 both in one PR, since a data-layer-only PR is exactly the failure mode this rewrite exists to prevent.\n\nConfirmed response shape (`src/chain-stake-transfers.mjs`, `src/openapi-sample.mjs:752-800`):\n```\n{\n  schema_version: number,\n  window: string | null,\n  observed_at: string | null,\n  subnet_count: number,\n  network: { distinct_senders: number, transfers: number, transfers_per_sender: number | null },\n  intensity_distribution: { count, mean, min, p25, median, p75, p90, max } | null,\n  subnets: [{ netuid: number, distinct_senders: number, transfers: number, transfers_per_sender: number | null }]\n}\n```\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/types.ts` \u2014 add a `ChainStakeTransfers` interface matching the shape above (sibling of `SubnetStakeTransfers`, line 1200; model on `ChainTransferPairs`, line 1648)\n- `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` \u2014 add `normalizeChainStakeTransfers(raw)` + `chainStakeTransfersQuery(window = \"7d\", limit = 20)`, following `chainTransferPairsQuery` (lines 2439-2458) exactly: `queryOptions`, `queryKey: k(\"chain-stake-transfers\", window, limit)`, `apiFetch<Partial<ChainStakeTransfers>>(\"/api/v1/chain/stake-transfers\", { params: { window, limit }, signal })`, `staleTime: STALE_MED`\n- `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` \u2014 extend `ExplorerDashboard()`. Anchor: add the new `useSuspenseQuery(chainStakeTransfersQuery(win))` call alongside the existing `activity`/`fees`/`calls`/`signers` suspense reads (lines 230-233), reusing the page's existing `win` search param (`explorerSearchSchema`, lines 26-28, already `7d`/`30d` \u2014 matches the endpoint's supported windows exactly) so no new UI toggle is needed\n- What to render: a new `<section className=\"rounded-lg border border-border bg-card p-5\">` following the exact \"Top fee payers\" idiom already in this file (lines 401-451) \u2014 a header with a count badge (`{subnets.length} subnets`), then a `<table>` with columns Subnet / Transfers / Distinct senders / Transfers per sender, each subnet row linking to `/subnets/$netuid` (numeric `netuid` param, confirmed pattern at `index.tsx:732/773/877`) via `<Link to=\"/subnets/$netuid\" params={{ netuid: s.netuid }}>`. Surface the `network` rollup (total transfers, true distinct senders) as a one-line caption in the section header, matching how `fees.top_fee_payers.length` is shown as a caption today (line 406-408)\n- Coordination note: #3468 (stake-moves / within-account re-delegation) is the explicit \"distinct from\" twin named in this issue's own scope \u2014 keep the two leaderboards as separate sections so a reviewer isn't surprised by two similarly-shaped PRs touching `explorer.tsx` in the same area. #3475 (native-TAO transfers) and the already-shipped #3476 (transfer-pairs) also add sections to this same file \u2014 expect adjacent-section merge conflicts if worked in parallel\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Diff touches `apps/ui/src/routes/explorer.tsx` (not just `queries.ts`/`types.ts`)\n- [ ] `apps/ui/src/lib/metagraphed/queries.ts` adds `chainStakeTransfersQuery` and the component calls it via `useSuspenseQuery` (matching the page's existing suspense-read convention)\n- [ ] The new section renders a per-subnet leaderboard table (netuid, transfers, distinct senders, transfers-per-sender) ranked as returned by the API, each subnet linking to `/subnets/$netuid`\n- [ ] The network-wide rollup (`network.transfers`, `network.distinct_senders`) is visible in the section (header caption or inline stat), not just the per-subnet rows\n- [ ] Loading + empty + error states match this file's existing convention: the whole dashboard is wrapped in `Suspense`/`QueryErrorBoundary` (lines 72-76) for loading/error, and a cold/empty `subnets: []` response renders a plain `<p className=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-muted\">` fallback message, exactly like the \"No fee payers in this window yet.\" / \"No signers in this window yet.\" sibling sections (lines 447-449, 514)\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Do not implement the within-account re-delegation (`/chain/stake-moves`) leaderboard \u2014 that is #3468, a separate section/PR\n- Do not add a new window-selector control \u2014 reuse the page's existing `7d`/`30d` toggle\n- Do not touch the per-subnet `/api/v1/subnets/{netuid}/stake-transfers` route or its existing `subnetStakeTransfersQuery` \u2014 that data layer is already done and out of scope here\n\n## Size\n\nSize: S \u2014 keep this PR small (aim for \u226410 files / \u22641000 LOC).\n\nPart of #2542.",
